=== meta ===
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
issue: 419
title: a changed C extension is still opaque, and opaque evidence no longer holds a weakened Python assertion at warn
origin: successor of c_extension_still_opaque_neg with the same inputs, re-pinned by the #419 ruling
origin2: (issuecomment-6170353038: Q1 (b), Q5 (b), rule 2). ASSERT_WEAKENED in a Python test refuses
origin3: opaque-change evidence, so the `+ 0` in src/app/_speedups.c no longer explains `== 6` -> `> 0`,
origin4: and the reason names the opaque change. The old name now pins the expectation-family sibling.
=== before: src/app/_speedups.c ===
int add(int a, int b) { return a + b; }
=== after: src/app/_speedups.c ===
int add(int a, int b) { return a + b + 0; }
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app import total


def test_total():
    assert total(3) == 6
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app import total


def test_total():
    assert total(3) > 0
